## Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust the values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Settings are resolved with the following precedence, highest first:

1. Real environment variables (`APP__APP_NAME=...`)
1. `.env.local` — personal overrides, never committed
1. `.env` — your local base, never committed
1. Defaults declared in `src/{{ package_name }}/settings.py`

`.env.example` is the committed contract listing every supported key; every other `.env` file is gitignored and missing ones are ignored at load time. Deployed environments set real environment variables rather than shipping `.env` files, and secrets mounted as files under `/run/secrets` (Docker, Kubernetes) are picked up automatically.

Unknown keys in an env file are ignored, so `.env` can be shared with other tooling, but a misspelled `APP__`/`LOGGING__` key fails at startup.

## Development

```bash
uv run pytest                       # run tests
uv run ruff check .                 # lint
uv run ruff format .                # format
uv run ty check src/ tests/         # type check
uv run pre-commit run --all-files   # run all hooks
```

### Docs

```bash
uv sync --extra docs                # install docs dependencies
uv run mkdocs serve                 # serve docs locally at http://127.0.0.1:8000
uv run mkdocs build                 # build static site into site/
```
